---
import Shader14 from "../components/Shader14.astro";
import SeoHead from "../components/SeoHead.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#000000" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" sizes="any" href="/favicon.svg?v=1" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <SeoHead
      title="Monarchic LLC | MCP tools for agent teams"
      description="Monarchic LLC builds MCP products for repository intelligence, durable memory, browser checks, and evidence-heavy agent workflows."
      path="/"
    />
  </head>
  <body class="min-h-screen bg-black text-white">
    <main class="relative min-h-screen overflow-hidden">
      <Shader14
        className="pointer-events-none fixed inset-0 h-full w-full opacity-75"
      />
      <div class="pointer-events-none fixed inset-0 bg-[linear-gradient(to_bottom,_rgba(0,0,0,0.62),_rgba(0,0,0,0.94))]"></div>

      <section class="relative z-10 mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-8 sm:py-12">
        <header class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-5 border-b-2 border-white pb-6">
          <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-3">
            <img
              src="/favicon.svg"
              alt="Monarchic LLC logo"
              class="h-9 w-9 bg-white object-cover p-1"
              width="36"
              height="36"
            />
            <span class="text-[0.7rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.36em] text-white/72">
              Monarchic LLC
            </span>
          </a>
          <nav class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <a href="/products" class="border-2 border-white px-4 py-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] transition hover:bg-white hover:text-black">Products</a>
            <a href="/research" class="border-2 border-white px-4 py-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] transition hover:bg-white hover:text-black">Research</a>
          </nav>
        </header>

        <section class="grid min-h-[calc(100vh-112px)] gap-10 py-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.15fr_0.85fr] lg:items-center">
          <div>
            <p class="mb-5 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.4em] text-white/64">
              Monarchic LLC
            </p>
            <h1 class="max-w-5xl text-5xl font-extrabold uppercase leading-[0.9] sm:text-7xl lg:text-8xl [text-shadow:6px_6px_0_rgba(255,255,255,0.12)]">
              MCP Tools<br />For Agent Work
            </h1>
            <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-base leading-8 text-white/78 sm:text-lg">
              Monarchic LLC is building the tool layer for serious agent
              workflows. The larger Monarchic platform is where this is headed,
              but the focus right now is the MCP catalog: RepoIntel for codebase
              context, ExplicitMem for durable memory, BrowserOps for browser
              checks, and more.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
              <a
                href="/products"
                class="inline-flex items-center justify-center border-2 border-white bg-white px-5 py-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-black transition hover:bg-black hover:text-white"
              >
                Products
              </a>
              <a
                href="/research"
                class="inline-flex items-center justify-center border-2 border-white px-5 py-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.28em] transition hover:bg-white hover:text-black"
              >
                Research
              </a>
              <a
                href="/products"
                class="inline-flex items-center justify-center border-2 border-cyan-300 px-5 py-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-cyan-200 transition hover:bg-cyan-200 hover:text-black"
              >
                Join Waitlist
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="grid gap-4">
            <div class="border-2 border-white bg-black/72 p-5">
              <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.32em] text-cyan-200">MCP Catalog</p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-white/74">
                The current product surface is a set of MCPs for memory,
                repository context, browser checks, release evidence, and other
                agent workflows.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="border-2 border-white bg-black/72 p-5">
              <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.32em] text-amber-200">Bigger Direction</p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-white/74">
                Monarchic is the larger autonomous development platform we are
                building toward. It is not available today.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="border-2 border-white bg-black/72 p-5">
              <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.32em] text-emerald-200">Research</p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-white/74">
                Research pages show benchmark scope, receipts, and the parts we
                are not claiming yet. Scores need context.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="grid gap-5 border-t-2 border-white py-10 md:grid-cols-3">
          <a href="/products/mcp-repointel" class="group border border-white/58 bg-black/64 p-5 transition hover:bg-white hover:text-black">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-white/52 group-hover:text-black/52">RepoIntel</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-extrabold uppercase">Repository intelligence for agents</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-white/70 group-hover:text-black/70">
              Generated wiki context, dependency summaries, and targeted code evidence.
            </p>
          </a>
          <a href="/products/mcp-explicitmem" class="group border border-white/58 bg-black/64 p-5 transition hover:bg-white hover:text-black">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-white/52 group-hover:text-black/52">ExplicitMem</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-extrabold uppercase">Durable memory with receipts</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-white/70 group-hover:text-black/70">
              Typed memory, graph links, bounded recall, and audit-friendly retrieval.
            </p>
          </a>
          <a href="/products/mcp-browserops" class="group border border-white/58 bg-black/64 p-5 transition hover:bg-white hover:text-black">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-white/52 group-hover:text-black/52">BrowserOps</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-extrabold uppercase">Browser verification evidence</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-white/70 group-hover:text-black/70">
              Screenshots, console diagnostics, network checks, and scenario receipts.
            </p>
          </a>
        </section>

        <section class="grid gap-6 border-t-2 border-white py-10 lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr]">
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-white/54">Who It Is For</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-extrabold uppercase sm:text-4xl">
              For teams that need MCP tools with clearer boundaries, better
              evidence, and less one-off glue code.
            </h2>
          </div>
          <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
            <div class="border border-white/46 bg-black/64 p-4">
              <p class="text-sm font-extrabold uppercase">Account scoped</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-white/68">Routes and API keys belong to an account, not a loose demo token.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="border border-white/46 bg-black/64 p-4">
              <p class="text-sm font-extrabold uppercase">Proof included</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-white/68">Research and receipts say what each MCP proves and what it does not.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="border border-white/46 bg-black/64 p-4">
              <p class="text-sm font-extrabold uppercase">Coming soon</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-white/68">We are holding access until the account controls are boring and reliable.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="grid gap-6 border-t-2 border-white py-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr]">
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-white/54">Access</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 max-w-4xl text-3xl font-extrabold uppercase sm:text-4xl">
              Access opens when the hosted MCP routes, account setup, and
              receipts are ready to stand behind.
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-7 text-white/70">
              We are not publishing fixed pricing yet. For now, use the catalog
              to see what is coming and which MCPs already have research
              behind them.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="grid gap-3">
            <div class="border border-white/46 bg-black/64 p-4">
              <p class="text-sm font-extrabold uppercase">Environment</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-white/68">
                Know which repo, browser surface, memory scope, or account the
                MCP workflow will touch.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="border border-white/46 bg-black/64 p-4">
              <p class="text-sm font-extrabold uppercase">Evidence</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-white/68">
                Keep screenshots, logs, benchmark notes, and receipt files close
                to the work they support.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="border border-white/46 bg-black/64 p-4">
              <p class="text-sm font-extrabold uppercase">Handoff</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-white/68">
                Keep API access, billing, support, and rollback decisions tied
                to the same account.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="border-t-2 border-white py-10">
          <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr]">
            <div>
              <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-white/54">What You Get</p>
              <h2 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-3xl font-extrabold uppercase sm:text-4xl">
                Hosted MCP products, account ownership, and enough evidence to
                know what happened.
              </h2>
              <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-7 text-white/70">
                The point is to make agent tooling less opaque: what the tool
                did, what evidence it produced, and where the boundary sits.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
              <div class="border border-white/46 bg-black/64 p-4">
                <p class="text-sm font-extrabold uppercase">MCP access</p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-white/68">
                  A controlled surface for MCP tools, API keys, and target
                  environment notes.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="border border-white/46 bg-black/64 p-4">
                <p class="text-sm font-extrabold uppercase">Owner record</p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-white/68">
                  The account owner, support path, and rollback decision stay
                  attached to the same workspace.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="border border-white/46 bg-black/64 p-4">
                <p class="text-sm font-extrabold uppercase">Evidence pack</p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-white/68">
                  Screenshots, repository context, memory traces, logs, or
                  receipt files stay available for review.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="border border-white/46 bg-black/64 p-4">
                <p class="text-sm font-extrabold uppercase">Exit criteria</p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-white/68">
                  A clear place to decide whether to expand, change course, or
                  stop using a route.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="grid gap-6 border-t-2 border-white py-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1fr]">
          <div class="border border-white/46 bg-black/64 p-5">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-cyan-200">Good Fit</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">
              Teams preparing agent tools to touch real repositories, browsers,
              and customer workflows.
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-white/70">
              Join the waitlist when you need hosted MCP access, evidence you
              can inspect, and account-level control.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-white/46 bg-black/64 p-5">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-amber-200">Bad Fit</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">
              One-off demos, unaudited automations, or local tools that do not
              need account-level control.
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-white/70">
              Monarchic MCPs are for account-owned agent tooling. Local
              experimentation should stay local.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-5 border-t-2 border-white py-10 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-white/54">Next Step</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-3xl font-extrabold uppercase sm:text-4xl">
              Browse the catalog, read the research, and join the waitlist for
              the tools you care about.
            </h2>
          </div>
          <a
            href="/products"
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center border-2 border-cyan-300 px-5 py-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-cyan-200 transition hover:bg-cyan-200 hover:text-black"
          >
            Join Waitlist
          </a>
        </section>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
